index 0000000..4045e18
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/aurora-forest-api.md
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+# Aurora forest.1 (local fork)
+
+Opt-in `api = "0.1-aurora-forest.1"` extends lighting.2 with terrain contact
+depth and semantic leaves. It is not an upstream Horizon API. Previous pack
+versions retain their stage contracts and do not allocate a contact prepass.
+
+## Contract
+
+- `MaterialInput.is_leaves: bool`: true for faces of `Info.leaves` blocks
+  (the registry's LeavesBlock class), not inferred from texture colour.
+- Group 3 binding 4: `contact_depth: texture_depth_2d`. The helper
+  `contact_depth_at(uv)` uses nearest texel loads, with clamped coordinates.
+- The texture contains **this frame's** opaque/cutout terrain depth at world
+  render resolution. Reversed depth: 0 is empty, 1 is near. Use the frame's
+  inverse projection and inverse view to reconstruct camera-relative positions.
+- Available only to the material hook. Excludes translucent terrain, water,
+  entities, sky, hand and HUD. The existing pre-translucent snapshot is unchanged.
+
+The depth prepass runs before sky and material shading. It uses the same
+terrain camera, visible section/facing lists, UV decoding, sprite alpha cutoff
+of 0.5 and layer bit 0x8000 for forced opacity. It clears every frame and
+reallocates at resolution changes. There is no reprojection or temporal history.
+
+TerrainVertex remains 28 bytes. A cleared bit 0x40000000 in packed colour marks
+leaves; RGB, low-nibble emission and water bit 0x80000000 remain intact. Meshing
+sets the bit from block semantics. Legacy constructors remain non-leaf.
+
+## Forest Light prototype
+
+The pack evaluates 8 screen directions with 3 samples per direction within
+2.4 blocks (configurable 0.5–3), rejects coplanar/sky/distant samples and fades
+out at 40–64 blocks. It attenuates only linear sky/ground fill, before display
+mapping. Existing vertex AO, direct sun, local light and model lighting remain
+separate. Thin-leaf transmission uses a short offset sun-map query, with
+daylight, weather and skylight guards. This is an approximation, not GI.
+
+Screen-space contact shading cannot see off-screen occluders or hidden layers;
+entities do not participate. The extra terrain pass has a GPU/CPU cost even
+with contact strength set to zero. Switch to the lighting.2 baseline pack to
+measure total feature overhead. No performance claim before actual Metal tests.
+
+## Validation
+
+CPU: shader API contract tests, mesher metadata preservation, actual composed
+terrain/sky/entity WGSL validation, build, rustfmt and scoped Clippy.
+GPU fixture `contact_cutout_freshness_resize_on_gpu` reads back cutout versus
+forced-opaque depth, an empty next frame and two resolutions. Require an actual
+adapter with `AURORA_REQUIRE_GPU=1`; a skipped test is not a hardware pass.
+The preview also checks shadow/history/model fixtures and the full pack's
+pipelines before starting a new isolated world. Visual contact strength,
+leaf transmission, edge artifacts and total frame cost still require gameplay.
